WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.148
Ten thirty-five exchanges.

2
00:00:02.276 --> 00:00:06.548
Section ten thirty-five of the tax code lets an owner swap one contract for another

3
00:00:06.723 --> 00:00:09.102
without paying tax on the gain.

4
00:00:10.040 --> 00:00:11.351
Here's what's allowed.

5
00:00:11.712 --> 00:00:15.159
Life insurance for another life insurance policy: tax-free.

6
00:00:15.706 --> 00:00:17.992
Life insurance for an annuity: tax-free.

7
00:00:18.283 --> 00:00:20.778
One annuity for another annuity: tax-free.

8
00:00:20.907 --> 00:00:23.879
But an annuity for a life insurance policy is not allowed.

9
00:00:24.112 --> 00:00:29.502
Life insurance or an annuity can also be exchanged for a qualified long-term care

10
00:00:29.522 --> 00:00:30.670
policy.

11
00:00:31.596 --> 00:00:36.773
For a clean exchange, keep the same owner, and the same insured or annuitant.

12
00:00:37.436 --> 00:00:42.450
If the owner receives any cash in the exchange, called boot, that cash is taxable.

13
00:00:42.684 --> 00:00:46.182
And remember that a ten thirty-five exchange is still a replacement,

14
00:00:46.202 --> 00:00:48.558
so all the replacement rules apply.

15
00:00:49.495 --> 00:00:54.440
Here's the memory trick: you can move toward an annuity, but never away from it.

16
00:00:54.894 --> 00:00:59.227
Going from an annuity to life insurance would turn taxable annuity gains into a

17
00:00:59.247 --> 00:01:02.462
tax-free death benefit, so it isn't allowed.
